Chalo bhai, shuru karte hain **Day 1 — Topic 1: Data Types, Stack vs Heap Memory, aur Java Pass-by-Value (Array Trap)**.

Ismein hum 3 main words ka literal matlab clear karenge: **Primitive**, **Reference**, aur **Heap vs Stack**.

---

### 1. Primitives vs Reference Types (Data kahan rehta hai?)

Java mein data do tarah ka hota hai:

* **Primitive Types (8 hote hain):** `int`, `long`, `double`, `float`, `boolean`, `char`, `byte`, `short`.
* Inmein **seedhi value** store hoti hai (jaise `int x = 10;`).
* Yeh chhote aur fast hote hain, isliye **Stack** memory mein store hote hain.


* **Reference Types (Objects & Arrays):** `String`, `int[]` (Array), `HashMap`, ya tumhari banayi hui koi bhi `Class` (jaise `User`).
* Inka actual data bada hota hai, isliye woh **Heap** memory mein banta hai.
* Variable ke andar actual data nahi, balki us Heap memory ka **address (reference)** store hota hai.



---

### 2. Stack vs Heap (Literal Matlab)

Jab Java program chalta hai, toh RAM ka kuch hissa JVM ko milta hai, jise do main parts mein baanta jaata hai:

1. **Stack Memory (Temporary & Fast):**
* Jab bhi koi method (jaise `main()`) call hota hai, Stack mein uske liye ek chhota block (Stack Frame) banta hai.
* Ismein **local primitive variables** (`int a = 5`) aur **object ke references (addresses)** rakhe jaate hain.
* Jaise hi method khatam hota hai, uska Stack block turant delete ho jaata hai.


2. **Heap Memory (Global & Dynamic):**
* Jab bhi tum **`new`** keyword likhte ho (jaise `new int[3]` ya `new HashMap<>()`), toh woh object **Heap** mein banta hai.
* Heap tab tak clean nahi hota jab tak **Garbage Collector (GC)** un unused objects ko delete na kare.



---

### 3. The Classic Interview Trap: Java Pass-by-Value (Array / Pointer Sawal)

Java mein C/C++ jaise pointers (`*ptr`, `&x`) nahi hote, aur **Java hamesha 100% Pass-by-Value hota hai**.

* Agar tum primitive (`int x = 10`) method mein bhejte ho, toh `10` ki ek **copy** jaati hai. Original `x` nahi badalta.
* Agar tum Array ya Object (`int[] arr`) method mein bhejte ho, toh **Heap ke address (reference) ki ek copy** jaati hai! Kyunki dono variables (original aur copy) Heap mein **ek hi array** ko point kar rahe hote hain, isliye andar ki value badalne par original array bhi badal jaata hai!

